<title>SRI LANKA: Lanka Ceramic falls on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Lanka Ceramic falls on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profit-taking by retail investors pulled down shares of Lanka Ceramic Ltd by 2.56 percent or one rupee to 38 in early Friday trade, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Small investors who bought the share up from around 30 rupees in early April are taking profits,&quot; said a local broker. The share rose with the market's upward movement on improved investor sentiment.</p>
<p>Percieved political stability, improved money supply and easing interest rates have led to market optimism lately.</p>
<p>-- Colombo Newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
